msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/workflows/pipelines.md:154
msgid "Python Processing Pipeline — `client.pipeline(...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/workflows/pipelines.md:156
msgid ""
"A different capability from the YAML orchestration above: a **chainable "
"builder** over the processing operations documented throughout "
"[Preprocessing Engine](../processing/optical/preprocessing.md), [Spectral "
"Indices](../processing/optical/spectral-indices.md), "
"[Postprocessing](../processing/optical/postprocessing.md), and [SAR "
"Processing](../processing/sar-insar/sar.md) — for processing files you "
"already have, not for search/download orchestration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/workflows/pipelines.md:180
msgid ""
"Each step's output feeds directly into the next step as input — a chain, not"
" independent calls that happen to be written sequentially. `.run(input=...)`"
" executes every queued step in order and returns a `PipelineRunResult` with "
"per-step status, output paths, and timing."
msgstr ""

